{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ror7pNLi1GvXNoWfzzi5Ew","type":"tool_result","content":"1027\tdef rotate_if_needed(log_path: Path, threshold_bytes: int) -> Optional[Path]:\n1028\t    \"\"\"Rename log_path to a monthly rotated file if it exceeds the threshold.\n1029\t\n1030\t    Must be called UNDER the lock so no concurrent writer can race.\n1031\t\n1032\t    PLAN-045 Wave 2 P0-08: delegates to ``_lib.audit_rotation.rotate_if_needed``\n1033\t    so both write paths (this ``append_entry`` + ``_lib.audit_emit._write_event``)\n1034\t    share identical rotation semantics. Preserves the existing call\n1035\t    signature for backwards compatibility.\n1036\t\n1037\t    PLAN-044 audit-v2 C6-P0-02 fix (Wave B): on successful rotation,\n1038\t    invoke ``audit_hmac.reset_chain_on_rotation()`` so the HMAC chain\n1039\t    starts a fresh genesis on the new log file. Without this, rotated\n1040\t    logs continue chain from the previous final hmac into the new\n1041\t    file's genesis row, which `audit-verify-chain.py` cannot validate\n1042\t    (genesis is by definition prev_hmac=GENESIS_PREV; a non-genesis\n1043\t    prev_hmac after rotation looks like silent tamper). Pattern was\n1044\t    already correct in ``_lib.audit_emit._write_event`` — Wave B brings\n1045\t    ``audit_log.py`` to parity.\n1046\t\n1047\t    Returns the rotated path if rotation happened, None otherwise.\n1048\t    \"\"\"\n1049\t    try:\n1050\t        from _lib.audit_rotation import rotate_if_needed as _shared_rotate\n1051\t    except ImportError:\n1052\t        # Defensive: if the shared primitive isn't available (partial\n1053\t        # install), fall back to the inlined legacy implementation so\n1054\t        # rotation still works in the classic path.\n1055\t        rotated = _legacy_rotate_inline(log_path, threshold_bytes)\n1056\t    else:\n1057\t        rotated = _shared_rotate(log_path, threshold_bytes, now_month_slug())\n1058\t\n1059\t    # PLAN-044 audit-v2 C6-P0-02 — reset the per-process HMAC chain\n1060\t    # state so the next entry written to the fresh log file is a\n1061\t    # GENESIS_PREV-rooted row. Best-effort: missing _lib.audit_hmac\n1062\t    # is non-fatal (older installs); chain integrity tests will catch\n1063\t    # any rotated row that violates the genesis rule.\n1064\t    if rotated is not None:\n1065\t        try:\n1066\t            from _lib import audit_hmac as _audit_hmac\n1067\t            if hasattr(_audit_hmac, \"reset_chain_on_rotation\"):\n1068\t                _audit_hmac.reset_chain_on_rotation()\n1069\t        except Exception:\n1070\t            pass\n1071\t    return rotated\n1072\t\n1073\t\n1074\tdef _legacy_rotate_inline(\n1075\t    log_path: Path, threshold_bytes: int\n1076\t) -> Optional[Path]:\n1077\t    \"\"\"Fallback rotation for the rare case ``_lib.audit_rotation`` is missing.\n1078\t\n1079\t    Kept in-line so a half-installed framework still rotates. Mirrors\n1080\t    the behavior of the shared primitive byte-for-byte.\n1081\t    \"\"\"\n1082\t    try:\n1083\t        if not log_path.is_file():\n1084\t            return None\n1085\t        size = log_path.stat().st_size\n1086\t        if size <= threshold_bytes:\n1087\t            return None\n1088\t    except OSError:\n1089\t        return None\n1090\t\n1091\t    month = now_month_slug()\n1092\t    base = log_path.parent / f\"{log_path.stem}-{month}.jsonl\"\n1093\t    candidate = base\n1094\t    counter = 1\n1095\t    while candidate.exists():\n1096\t        candidate = log_path.parent / f\"{log_path.stem}-{month}-{counter}.jsonl\"\n1097\t        counter += 1\n1098\t        if counter > 1000:\n1099\t            return None\n1100\t\n1101\t    try:\n1102\t        os.replace(str(log_path), str(candidate))\n1103\t    except OSError:\n1104\t        return None\n1105\t    return candidate\n1106\t\n1107\t\n1108\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1109\t# Error breadcrumb\n1110\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1111\t\n1112\t\n1113\tdef write_breadcrumb(err_path: Path, message: str) -> None:\n1114\t    \"\"\"Best-effort write to the errors log. Never raises.\"\"\"\n1115\t    try:\n1116\t        err_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n1117\t        ts = now_iso_utc()\n1118\t        with open(err_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n1119\t            f.write(f\"[{ts}] {message}\\n\")\n1120\t    except OSError:\n1121\t        # Last-resort: stderr\n1122\t        try:\n1123\t            sys.stderr.write(f\"[audit-log] breadcrumb write failed: {message}\\n\")\n1124\t        except Exception:  # pragma: no cover\n1125\t            pass\n1126\t\n1127\t\n1128\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1129\t# PLAN-045 F-01-06 — symlink + ownership defense\n1130\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1131\t\n1132\t\n1133\tdef _is_safe_audit_path(\n1134\t    path: Path, expected_uid: int\n1135\t) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n1136\t    \"\"\"Check audit path for symlink + ownership safety.\n1137\t\n1138\t    Returns ``(True, \"\")`` if safe (nonexistent OR real file/dir owned\n1139\t    by ``expected_uid``). Returns ``(False, reason)`` if unsafe\n1140\t    (symlink OR owner mismatch).\n1141\t\n1142\t    Uses ``os.lstat`` (not ``stat``) so symlinks themselves are\n1143\t    inspected rather than their targets. Never raises.\n1144\t\n1145\t    ## Threat model\n1146\t\n1147\t    1. **Symlink redirection.** An attacker with write access to\n1148\t       ``$HOME/.claude/projects/`` creates\n1149\t       ``ceo-orchestration -> /tmp/evil``. Every append goes to\n1150\t       attacker-controlled path, defeats tamper-evident audit trail.\n1151\t    2. **UID squatting.** Another user's process creates the audit\n1152\t       directory. Hook runs as current user → fails to open for\n1153\t       append (EACCES) OR leaks sensitive data into foreign-owned\n1154\t       file if perms are too permissive.\n1155\t\n1156\t    Both are refused before any write. The caller logs a breadcrumb\n1157\t    to the /tmp fallback path and returns silently (fail-open on\n1158\t    session; forensic trail preserved).\n1159\t    \"\"\"\n1160\t    try:\n1161\t        st = path.lstat()\n1162\t    except FileNotFoundError:\n1163\t        # Nonexistent is safe — the normal first-write path.\n1164\t        return (True, \"\")\n1165\t    except OSError as e:\n1166\t        return (False, f\"lstat_error:{e.__class__.__name__}\")\n1167\t    if stat.S_ISLNK(st.st_mode):\n1168\t        return (False, \"symlink_rejected\")\n1169\t    if st.st_uid != expected_uid:\n1170\t        return (\n1171\t            False,\n1172\t            f\"uid_mismatch:owner={st.st_uid} proc={expected_uid}\",\n1173\t        )\n1174\t    return (True, \"\")\n1175\t\n1176\t\n1177\tdef _fallback_security_breadcrumb(message: str) -> None:\n1178\t    \"\"\"Breadcrumb to ``/tmp`` fallback when primary audit dir is unsafe.\n1179\t\n1180\t    Mirrors ``_lib.audit_emit._fallback_log_path`` pattern. Never\n1181\t    raises. Writes under the current user's namespaced filename so\n1182\t    multi-user systems don't clobber each other.\n1183\t    \"\"\"\n1184\t    try:\n1185\t        try:\n1186\t            user = getpass.getuser() or \"unknown\"\n1187\t        except Exception:\n1188\t            user = os.environ.get(\"USER\") or \"unknown\"\n1189\t        user = \"\".join(\n1190\t            c for c in user if c.isalnum() or c in (\"-\", \"_\", \".\")\n1191\t        )\n1192\t        fallback = Path(\"/tmp\") / f\"ceo-audit-fallback-{user}.log\"\n1193\t        ts = now_iso_utc()\n1194\t        with open(fallback, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n1195\t            f.write(f\"[{ts}] audit-log security: {message}\\n\")\n1196\t    except Exception:\n1197\t        pass\n1198\t\n1199\t\n1200\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1201\t# Append entry under lock\n1202\t# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1203\t\n1204\t\n1205\tdef append_entry(\n1206\t    entry: Dict[str, Any],"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b95297ab-5d0d-413e-87dc-83b93d304a3d","uuid":"65b003de-07e3-4342-af99-e41efa76b384","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:33:03.058Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-182/staged-w1/tree/.claude/hooks/audit_log.py","content":"def rotate_if_needed(log_path: Path, threshold_bytes: int) -> Optional[Path]:\n    \"\"\"Rename log_path to a monthly rotated file if it exceeds the threshold.\n\n    Must be called UNDER the lock so no concurrent writer can race.\n\n    PLAN-045 Wave 2 P0-08: delegates to ``_lib.audit_rotation.rotate_if_needed``\n    so both write paths (this ``append_entry`` + ``_lib.audit_emit._write_event``)\n    share identical rotation semantics. Preserves the existing call\n    signature for backwards compatibility.\n\n    PLAN-044 audit-v2 C6-P0-02 fix (Wave B): on successful rotation,\n    invoke ``audit_hmac.reset_chain_on_rotation()`` so the HMAC chain\n    starts a fresh genesis on the new log file. Without this, rotated\n    logs continue chain from the previous final hmac into the new\n    file's genesis row, which `audit-verify-chain.py` cannot validate\n    (genesis is by definition prev_hmac=GENESIS_PREV; a non-genesis\n    prev_hmac after rotation looks like silent tamper). Pattern was\n    already correct in ``_lib.audit_emit._write_event`` — Wave B brings\n    ``audit_log.py`` to parity.\n\n    Returns the rotated path if rotation happened, None otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        from _lib.audit_rotation import rotate_if_needed as _shared_rotate\n    except ImportError:\n        # Defensive: if the shared primitive isn't available (partial\n        # install), fall back to the inlined legacy implementation so\n        # rotation still works in the classic path.\n        rotated = _legacy_rotate_inline(log_path, threshold_bytes)\n    else:\n        rotated = _shared_rotate(log_path, threshold_bytes, now_month_slug())\n\n    # PLAN-044 audit-v2 C6-P0-02 — reset the per-process HMAC chain\n    # state so the next entry written to the fresh log file is a\n    # GENESIS_PREV-rooted row. Best-effort: missing _lib.audit_hmac\n    # is non-fatal (older installs); chain integrity tests will catch\n    # any rotated row that violates the genesis rule.\n    if rotated is not None:\n        try:\n            from _lib import audit_hmac as _audit_hmac\n            if hasattr(_audit_hmac, \"reset_chain_on_rotation\"):\n                _audit_hmac.reset_chain_on_rotation()\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    return rotated\n\n\ndef _legacy_rotate_inline(\n    log_path: Path, threshold_bytes: int\n) -> Optional[Path]:\n    \"\"\"Fallback rotation for the rare case ``_lib.audit_rotation`` is missing.\n\n    Kept in-line so a half-installed framework still rotates. Mirrors\n    the behavior of the shared primitive byte-for-byte.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        if not log_path.is_file():\n            return None\n        size = log_path.stat().st_size\n        if size <= threshold_bytes:\n            return None\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n\n    month = now_month_slug()\n    base = log_path.parent / f\"{log_path.stem}-{month}.jsonl\"\n    candidate = base\n    counter = 1\n    while candidate.exists():\n        candidate = log_path.parent / f\"{log_path.stem}-{month}-{counter}.jsonl\"\n        counter += 1\n        if counter > 1000:\n            return None\n\n    try:\n        os.replace(str(log_path), str(candidate))\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n    return candidate\n\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Error breadcrumb\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef write_breadcrumb(err_path: Path, message: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort write to the errors log. Never raises.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        err_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        ts = now_iso_utc()\n        with open(err_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(f\"[{ts}] {message}\\n\")\n    except OSError:\n        # Last-resort: stderr\n        try:\n            sys.stderr.write(f\"[audit-log] breadcrumb write failed: {message}\\n\")\n        except Exception:  # pragma: no cover\n            pass\n\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAN-045 F-01-06 — symlink + ownership defense\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _is_safe_audit_path(\n    path: Path, expected_uid: int\n) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n    \"\"\"Check audit path for symlink + ownership safety.\n\n    Returns ``(True, \"\")`` if safe (nonexistent OR real file/dir owned\n    by ``expected_uid``). Returns ``(False, reason)`` if unsafe\n    (symlink OR owner mismatch).\n\n    Uses ``os.lstat`` (not ``stat``) so symlinks themselves are\n    inspected rather than their targets. Never raises.\n\n    ## Threat model\n\n    1. **Symlink redirection.** An attacker with write access to\n       ``$HOME/.claude/projects/`` creates\n       ``ceo-orchestration -> /tmp/evil``. Every append goes to\n       attacker-controlled path, defeats tamper-evident audit trail.\n    2. **UID squatting.** Another user's process creates the audit\n       directory. Hook runs as current user → fails to open for\n       append (EACCES) OR leaks sensitive data into foreign-owned\n       file if perms are too permissive.\n\n    Both are refused before any write. The caller logs a breadcrumb\n    to the /tmp fallback path and returns silently (fail-open on\n    session; forensic trail preserved).\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        st = path.lstat()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        # Nonexistent is safe — the normal first-write path.\n        return (True, \"\")\n    except OSError as e:\n        return (False, f\"lstat_error:{e.__class__.__name__}\")\n    if stat.S_ISLNK(st.st_mode):\n        return (False, \"symlink_rejected\")\n    if st.st_uid != expected_uid:\n        return (\n            False,\n            f\"uid_mismatch:owner={st.st_uid} proc={expected_uid}\",\n        )\n    return (True, \"\")\n\n\ndef _fallback_security_breadcrumb(message: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Breadcrumb to ``/tmp`` fallback when primary audit dir is unsafe.\n\n    Mirrors ``_lib.audit_emit._fallback_log_path`` pattern. Never\n    raises. Writes under the current user's namespaced filename so\n    multi-user systems don't clobber each other.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        try:\n            user = getpass.getuser() or \"unknown\"\n        except Exception:\n            user = os.environ.get(\"USER\") or \"unknown\"\n        user = \"\".join(\n            c for c in user if c.isalnum() or c in (\"-\", \"_\", \".\")\n        )\n        fallback = Path(\"/tmp\") / f\"ceo-audit-fallback-{user}.log\"\n        ts = now_iso_utc()\n        with open(fallback, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(f\"[{ts}] audit-log security: {message}\\n\")\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Append entry under lock\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef append_entry(\n    entry: Dict[str, Any],","numLines":180,"startLine":1027,"totalLines":1616}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ror7pNLi1GvXNoWfzzi5Ew","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
